Street pavement widths shall be as follows:
(1) Regional thoroughfares, 68 feet; major thoroughfares, 64 feet; secondary thoroughfares, 52 feet; and collector streets, 34 feet as given in the street and traffic plan of the city. This is not intended to prevent the city through its city council, from using stage development to accomplish the final conformance with these standards;
(2) Minor streets, 32 feet if curbs are to be used; 24 feet without curb and gutter;
(3) Cul-de-sac or dead-end streets, 28 feet if curbs are to be used; 24 feet without curb and gutter; and
(4) Alleys, 16 feet.
(Code 1958, § 20A-1202; Code 1991, § 17-139)

1049:
Maximum and minimum street and ditch grades shall be as follows:
(1) Regional thoroughfares, major thoroughfares, secondary thoroughfares as shown on the street and traffic plan of the city, not in excess of seven percent;
(2) Collector streets, not in excess of ten percent;
(3) Minor streets and dead-end streets and alleys, not in excess of 14 percent;
(4) No street grade shall be less than one-half of one percent.
(Code 1958, § 20A-1203; Code 1991, § 17-140)

